<title>CANADA: Canada government cash balances rise in week.</title>
<headline>Canada government cash balances rise in week.</headline>
<dateline>OTTAWA 1997-02-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>- The government of Canada's cash balances rose in the week that ended February 5, the Bank of Canada said on Friday.</p>
<p>				     Wk to Feb 5  Chg on wk Chg on yr</p>
<p>Notes in circulation		  26.85   +0.104    +0.707</p>
<p>Government cash balances	     5.97   +3.334    +0.134</p>
<p>Govt securities outstanding	461.99   +0.814    +7.671</p>
<p>Treasury bills			 131.15   -0.050   -27.950</p>
<p>Canada savings bonds		  33.25   -0.120    +2.127</p>
<p>All figures in billions of dollars. </p>
<p>   Chartered bank assets			 Dec	   Nov</p>
<p>   Net foreign currency			-13.81	-12.67</p>
<p>   Canadian dollar			     681.94	678.44</p>
<p>   Total Canadian liquid assets	    108.04	109.17</p>
<p>					   Dec 96     Nov 96     Dec 95</p>
<p>M1					  69.74	67.19	61.47</p>
<p>M2					 398.32     397.35     388.64</p>
<p>M3					 500.53     498.68     474.12</p>
<p>Note - Figures are unadjusted, in billions of dollars.</p>
<p>((--Reuters Ottawa Bureau (613) 235-6745))</p>
</text>
